+\revminor{To normalize by the seasonal climatological mean, each seasonal RMSE was divided by the training-period mean precipitation of that season, estimated from the 18,410 raw training timestamps (0.1052, 0.0854, 0.1125 and 0.1228~mm\,h$^{-1}$ for DJF, MAM, JJA and SON). Across the six models of the $W=6$ rerun set, NRMSE ranged from 2.65 to 2.83 in DJF, 2.03 to 2.14 in MAM, 2.19 to 2.40 in JJA and 2.07 to 2.22 in SON, compared with 2.97, 2.31, 2.51 and 2.32 for month-by-hour climatology (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3season_nrmse}). Every model had lower seasonal RMSE than this climatology in all five seeds, with seed-t and moving-block intervals excluding zero (Supplementary Table~\ref{supp-stab:r3season_clim_pairs}). NRMSE scales error by typical seasonal precipitation and is distinct from the skill score. Test-period mean precipitation exceeded the training mean in DJF (0.1440~mm\,h$^{-1}$) and fell below it in MAM (0.0685~mm\,h$^{-1}$); with test-period means as denominators, the positions of DJF and MAM reverse (1.93--2.07 and 2.53--2.67). With two to three realizations of each season in the test period, these differences describe the test years and do not establish a general seasonal ranking.}
 
