 \ReviewerComment{Section 4.1: Could you please show RMSE across 4 seasons normalized by the climatological mean for the season?}
 
-\PendingResponse
+\AuthorResponse{We thank the reviewer for this request. We now report, for DJF, MAM, JJA and SON, the RMSE of all six learning models and three references together with the RMSE normalized by the seasonal climatological mean (NRMSE). The normalizing mean for each season is the training-period mean precipitation of that season (18,410 raw training timestamps; 0.1052, 0.0854, 0.1125 and 0.1228~mm\,h$^{-1}$), so no test information enters the main definition; NRMSE based on test-period seasonal means is given only as a sensitivity. Model NRMSE ranged from 2.65--2.83 (DJF), 2.03--2.14 (MAM), 2.19--2.40 (JJA) and 2.07--2.22 (SON), below month-by-hour climatology in each season (2.97, 2.31, 2.51 and 2.32). All six models had lower RMSE than this climatology in every season and in all five seeds, with seed-based and moving-block intervals excluding zero. Because each season has only two to three realizations in the test period, and the DJF and MAM test-period means differed from their training means, the seasonal ordering is descriptive and changes under the test-mean normalization. The results are reported in Section~\ref{manuscript-sec:seasonal_baseline_check} and Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r3season_nrmse} and~\ref{supp-stab:r3season_clim_pairs}.}
 
